(function () {
  var m = {"MAM224": {"abstract": "With 2,300 components and over 700,000 dependencies, FINRA uses Kiro and AWS Transform custom to deploy GenAI upgrade agents across Python, Java, and Angular. Learn how governed automation and monthly \"Transform-a-thons\" reclaimed 1,800 engineering hours across 25 teams in three months, and how to shift from reactive patching to predictable dependency lifecycle management. Discover how FINRA's move to continuous modernization reduces the effort of maintaining technical debt.", "language": "en"},"MAM224-SC2": {"abstract": "With 2,300 components and over 700,000 dependencies, FINRA uses Kiro and AWS Transform custom to deploy GenAI upgrade agents across Python, Java, and Angular. Learn how governed automation and monthly \"Transform-a-thons\" reclaimed 1,800 engineering hours across 25 teams in three months, and how to shift from reactive patching to predictable dependency lifecycle management. Discover how FINRA's move to continuous modernization reduces the effort of maintaining technical debt.", "language": "en"},"MAM225": {"abstract": "AWS Transform for migrations is evolving to help enterprises tackle migration challenges head on. With agentic AI capabilities working across the migration lifecycle, AWS Transform automates what previously slowed teams down with manual work. In this session, get a first look at the latest capabilities accelerating your enterprise migration. Whether you're planning a first migration or scaling across hundreds of workloads, walk away knowing how agentic AI is changing how infrastructure migration is done and how you can put it in practice.", "language": "en"},"MAM225-SC2": {"abstract": "AWS Transform for migrations is evolving to help enterprises tackle migration challenges head on. With agentic AI capabilities working across the migration lifecycle, AWS Transform automates what previously slowed teams down with manual work. In this session, get a first look at the latest capabilities accelerating your enterprise migration. Whether you're planning a first migration or scaling across hundreds of workloads, walk away knowing how agentic AI is changing how infrastructure migration is done and how you can put it in practice.", "language": "en"},"MAM225-SC3": {"abstract": "AWS Transform for migrations is evolving to help enterprises tackle migration challenges head on. With agentic AI capabilities working across the migration lifecycle, AWS Transform automates what previously slowed teams down with manual work. In this session, get a first look at the latest capabilities accelerating your enterprise migration. Whether you're planning a first migration or scaling across hundreds of workloads, walk away knowing how agentic AI is changing how infrastructure migration is done and how you can put it in practice.", "language": "en"},"MAM226": {"abstract": "Running workloads across multiple clouds and on-premises data centers creates compounding complexity: inconsistent tooling, duplicated licensing costs, and operational overhead that slows everything down. HealthEdge faced exactly this across Azure, GCP, and four data centers while serving 130 health plans daily, where security is paramount. Hear how they're consolidating 8,700 servers via AWS Transform, 1,600 databases, and thousands of cloud services onto AWS on a 2-year roadmap, raising their security bar, and building internal AWS expertise to drive a lasting culture change - all without disrupting the plans that depend on them.", "language": "en"},"MAM227-S": {"abstract": "Enterprises are caught in a catch-22. Legacy estates must modernize to become AI-ready, yet the fastest path to AI runs through shared inference services where your transformation intelligence leaks to competitors. Modernize to build advantage & hand it away. Concierto's Sovereign Transformations breaks the bind. Ravi Kumar R, CTO, Trianz, presents a sovereign, unified platform that migrates, modernizes, manages, & prepares enterprises for agentic AI entirely within customer boundaries. Dual-engine architecture combines deterministic rules with private AI inference under oversight, all in your VPC. Intelligence compounds as a proprietary asset, sharpening transformations. Built on 100+ enterprises in 19 countries, Concierto delivers versatility at scale. Sovereign Transformations is an architectural choice about protecting and growing your intelligence solely for your company's benefit. This presentation is brought to you by Concierto by Trianz, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"MAM228": {"abstract": "Migration teams spend weeks per wave coordinating connectivity tests, performance comparisons, application health checks, and compliance reviews across disconnected tools. This lightning talk examines how to move post-deployment validation from a manual, multi-tool process into an integrated part of the migration workflow. You will learn approaches for automating infrastructure checks at deployment time, incorporating Well-Architected compliance into wave execution, and running day-one modernization actions so workloads land production-ready. Ideal for migration engineers and cloud architects managing large rehost and network modernization programs.", "language": "en"},"MAM229": {"abstract": "The biggest bottleneck in large-scale migrations isn't technical. It's the time between customer commitment and first workload moving. Agreements, partner funding approvals, and credit disbursement today require manual coordination across multiple teams and systems. AWS Transform automates the entire incentive lifecycle: one-click agreement acceptance, auto-populated partner fund requests, and threshold-based credit triggers that disburse automatically when tagged resources hit spend targets. In this session, learn how AWS Transform is removing administrative friction so incentives accelerate migrations instead of delaying them.", "language": "en"},"MAM230": {"abstract": "AI coding agents help developers ship more code than ever, but every new line adds dependencies, frameworks, and runtimes that will age into tech debt. Periodic \"modernization sprints\" can't keep up. In this session, learn how AWS Transform – continuous modernization makes code health a standing part of your software lifecycle, alongside build and deploy. See how it scans thousands of repositories in hours to find end-of-life dependencies, non-standard frameworks, and gaps that slow down AI agents. Then see how it remediates across your portfolio and monitors it as new issues appear. Learn how to define a transformation once and reuse it across your organization, and how customers cut tech debt assessment effort by over 60%. Leave with a practical path to keep your codebases modern, secure, and ready for AI.", "language": "en"},"MAM301": {"abstract": "This chalk talk presents a unified architecture spanning SAP Business Data Cloud, Databricks, Snowflake, and AWS-native services. Learn how AWS enables progressive modernization from zero-copy federation via BDC Connect, to Iceberg-based lakehouse architectures, to AI-powered analytics with Amazon Bedrock, SageMaker, and QuickSight. We introduce the AWS for SAP MCP Server, accessing OData services as AI-ready tools via Model Context Protocol. Live demos showcase AI agents resolving supply chain exceptions, generating Customer 360 insights, and accelerating BW modernization.", "language": "en"},"MAM305-R": {"abstract": "Migrating SQL Server databases with stored procedures, triggers, and complex T-SQL constructs to Aurora PostgreSQL typically takes weeks of manual schema conversion and dependency resolution. In this workshop, you'll walk through the end-to-end workflow using AWS Transform's agentic AI: assess your SQL Server database, automate schema conversion, resolve dependencies, then hand off to your local IDE where you review, refine, and deploy converted database objects directly. You'll leave knowing how to reduce weeks of manual effort to hours while improving conversion accuracy and confidence.", "language": "en"},"MAM305-R1": {"abstract": "Migrating SQL Server databases with stored procedures, triggers, and complex T-SQL constructs to Aurora PostgreSQL typically takes weeks of manual schema conversion and dependency resolution. In this workshop, you'll walk through the end-to-end workflow using AWS Transform's agentic AI: assess your SQL Server database, automate schema conversion, resolve dependencies, then hand off to your local IDE where you review, refine, and deploy converted database objects directly. You'll leave knowing how to reduce weeks of manual effort to hours while improving conversion accuracy and confidence.", "language": "en"},"MAM306-R": {"abstract": "You're planning a data center exit and need leadership to say yes. That means persuasive data, realistic cost estimates, and a proposal that makes financial sense. In this builders' session, you'll use AWS Transform's agentic AI capabilities paired with Discovery Agent data to assess your existing environment, generate cost estimates, and build a compelling business case for migration. You'll work through the end-to-end workflow from discovery and analysis to financial modeling, and leave ready to present a data-driven migration proposal to your stakeholders.", "language": "en"},"MAM306-R1": {"abstract": "You're planning a data center exit and need leadership to say yes. That means persuasive data, realistic cost estimates, and a proposal that makes financial sense. In this builders' session, you'll use AWS Transform's agentic AI capabilities paired with Discovery Agent data to assess your existing environment, generate cost estimates, and build a compelling business case for migration. You'll work through the end-to-end workflow from discovery and analysis to financial modeling, and leave ready to present a data-driven migration proposal to your stakeholders.", "language": "en"},"MAM307": {"abstract": "The cloud journey isn't just about migration anymore. It's about building intelligent frameworks that transform how organizations operate. In this gamified Experience-Based Acceleration (EBA) workshop, cross-functional teams compete in real time to architect migration and modernization solutions, build agentic AI workflows that automate at scale, and deploy AI-powered applications on AWS. Push boundaries, solve real challenges together, and have fun doing it. Walk away with battle-tested architectures, agentic automation patterns, and a cloud-fluent mindset your team can adopt immediately. Ready to play?", "language": "en"},"MAM308-R": {"abstract": "Migrating VMware or other on-premises environments to AWS involves dozens of coordinated steps, and most teams spend more time planning handoffs than actually moving workloads. In this workshop, you'll experience how AWS Transform's agentic AI orchestrates the full migration lifecycle: intelligent discovery, AI-driven wave planning, automated network translation, and server rehost execution. Specialized AI agents coordinate across each stage, making autonomous decisions while keeping you in control. You'll leave with hands-on experience using agentic AI to execute a real end-to-end multi-server migration. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM308-R1": {"abstract": "Migrating VMware or other on-premises environments to AWS involves dozens of coordinated steps, and most teams spend more time planning handoffs than actually moving workloads. In this workshop, you'll experience how AWS Transform's agentic AI orchestrates the full migration lifecycle: intelligent discovery, AI-driven wave planning, automated network translation, and server rehost execution. Specialized AI agents coordinate across each stage, making autonomous decisions while keeping you in control. You'll leave with hands-on experience using agentic AI to execute a real end-to-end multi-server migration. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM309-R": {"abstract": "Batch processing has powered critical enterprise workloads for decades, from mainframes running COBOL and PL/I to distributed systems on legacy Java. The trade-off? Overnight batch cycles that business processes can no longer afford. In this session, reimagine batch as event-driven microservices using Domain-Driven Design. AWS Transform reverse-engineers business rules from legacy code across platforms with full traceability, and Kiro translates that understanding into microservices specifications, generates production code, and creates Infrastructure as Code for AWS deployment. Leave with a repeatable pattern for reimagining batch workloads as real-time, event-driven microservices built on business rules that took decades to refine. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM309-R1": {"abstract": "Batch processing has powered critical enterprise workloads for decades, from mainframes running COBOL and PL/I to distributed systems on legacy Java. The trade-off? Overnight batch cycles that business processes can no longer afford. In this session, reimagine batch as event-driven microservices using Domain-Driven Design. AWS Transform reverse-engineers business rules from legacy code across platforms with full traceability, and Kiro translates that understanding into microservices specifications, generates production code, and creates Infrastructure as Code for AWS deployment. Leave with a repeatable pattern for reimagining batch workloads as real-time, event-driven microservices built on business rules that took decades to refine. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM310-R": {"abstract": "Enterprise data teams maintain ETL pipelines built on legacy tools like stored procedures, custom bash scripts, IBM DataStage and others, that resist migration due to undocumented dependencies. In this builders' session, use AWS Transform Custom to discover and map an existing ETL pipeline, generate a modernization blueprint, and rebuild it as a serverless workflow using AWS Glue and Step Functions. Each attendee picks one legacy source module (stored procedures, bash/SQL scripts, or DataStage jobs etc) and works hands-on through discovery, transformation logic analysis, and deploying a modernized pipeline.", "language": "en"},"MAM310-R1": {"abstract": "Enterprise data teams maintain ETL pipelines built on legacy tools like stored procedures, custom bash scripts, IBM DataStage and others, that resist migration due to undocumented dependencies. In this builders' session, use AWS Transform Custom to discover and map an existing ETL pipeline, generate a modernization blueprint, and rebuild it as a serverless workflow using AWS Glue and Step Functions. Each attendee picks one legacy source module (stored procedures, bash/SQL scripts, or DataStage jobs etc) and works hands-on through discovery, transformation logic analysis, and deploying a modernized pipeline.", "language": "en"},"MAM311-R": {"abstract": "You became a DBA, and now someone's asking you to be a cloud architect too. With over 240 AWS services, knowing where to start is half the battle. In this chalk talk, we'll map your core DBA tasks to AWS equivalents, covering networking, security, high availability, and disaster recovery for SQL Server. We'll also explore how AI-powered tools like Kiro and AWS Transform can accelerate your ramp-up, from intelligent code generation to modernizing .NET and SQL Server workloads. You'll leave with a clear path to choosing, securing, and cost-optimizing the right services. Come with questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM311-R1": {"abstract": "You became a DBA, and now someone's asking you to be a cloud architect too. With over 240 AWS services, knowing where to start is half the battle. In this chalk talk, we'll map your core DBA tasks to AWS equivalents, covering networking, security, high availability, and disaster recovery for SQL Server. We'll also explore how AI-powered tools like Kiro and AWS Transform can accelerate your ramp-up, from intelligent code generation to modernizing .NET and SQL Server workloads. You'll leave with a clear path to choosing, securing, and cost-optimizing the right services. Come with questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM312": {"abstract": "Migrating on-premises storage to AWS typically means weeks of manual assessment, business case building, and wave planning before a single byte moves. AWS Transform's agentic AI capabilities handle the full lifecycle, from automated assessment and business case generation to wave planning and execution, reducing that timeline to hours. In this lightning talk, see how to migrate storage from VMware estates, enterprise databases, and associated data with AI handling the complexity. Leave knowing how to start your first Transform project and accelerate time to results.", "language": "en"},"MAM313-R": {"abstract": "Migration and modernization involve dozens of manual steps across landing zones, networking, and containerization. What if you could drive the entire workflow from your IDE? In this code talk, you'll see how Kiro and AWS Transform work together as an agentic toolkit. First, generate a multi-account landing zone as infrastructure as code. Next, feed a VMware configuration export to the network agent and get Terraform modules or CDK constructs for VPCs, security groups, and production-ready network topology. Then point the containerization agent at a repo to produce ECR images and deploy to Amazon EKS.", "language": "en"},"MAM313-R1": {"abstract": "Migration and modernization involve dozens of manual steps across landing zones, networking, and containerization. What if you could drive the entire workflow from your IDE? In this code talk, you'll see how Kiro and AWS Transform work together as an agentic toolkit. First, generate a multi-account landing zone as infrastructure as code. Next, feed a VMware configuration export to the network agent and get Terraform modules or CDK constructs for VPCs, security groups, and production-ready network topology. Then point the containerization agent at a repo to produce ECR images and deploy to Amazon EKS.", "language": "en"},"MAM314": {"abstract": "Business-critical data scattered across Oracle, SQL Server, and VMware or Nutanix-hosted databases is the number one blocker to deploying agentic AI at scale. In this lightning talk, you'll get a practical playbook for database migration to AWS: real licensing challenges, cost optimization strategies, and modernization pathways that accelerate the path to cloud-native databases using AWS Transform and agentic AI. You'll leave with a clear migration framework that turns fragmented data estates into AI-ready infrastructure, no matter where your databases live today.", "language": "en"},"MAM315-R": {"abstract": "Not every app needs the same migration path, and figuring out which ones to rehost versus containerize is where teams get stuck. In this workshop, you'll use AWS Transform to plan a combined migration and modernization across your application portfolio, then execute a mix of container and rehost migrations deploying to Amazon ECS or EKS. You'll work through the full lifecycle. Learn how to order waves and coordinate cutover across a mixed portfolio. Leave with a realistic multi-wave plan you can apply to your own environment. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM315-R1": {"abstract": "Not every app needs the same migration path, and figuring out which ones to rehost versus containerize is where teams get stuck. In this workshop, you'll use AWS Transform to plan a combined migration and modernization across your application portfolio, then execute a mix of container and rehost migrations deploying to Amazon ECS or EKS. You'll work through the full lifecycle. Learn how to order waves and coordinate cutover across a mixed portfolio. Leave with a realistic multi-wave plan you can apply to your own environment. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM316-R": {"abstract": "Enterprise core applications were built for stability, not agentic AI. Tightly coupled dependencies across mainframe and interconnected systems make it nearly impossible to add intelligent capabilities without rearchitecting. In this workshop, take a legacy application through the full modernization journey: scope it, reverse-engineer existing behavior with AWS Transform, classify logic into deterministic microservices and AI agents, design target layers with Kiro, build the agentic layer on Amazon Bedrock and AgentCore, then deploy and validate. Leave with hands-on experience rebuilding a legacy application into an architecture ready for agentic AI. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM316-R1": {"abstract": "Enterprise core applications were built for stability, not agentic AI. Tightly coupled dependencies across mainframe and interconnected systems make it nearly impossible to add intelligent capabilities without rearchitecting. In this workshop, take a legacy application through the full modernization journey: scope it, reverse-engineer existing behavior with AWS Transform, classify logic into deterministic microservices and AI agents, design target layers with Kiro, build the agentic layer on Amazon Bedrock and AgentCore, then deploy and validate. Leave with hands-on experience rebuilding a legacy application into an architecture ready for agentic AI. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM317-R": {"abstract": "A monolithic traditional RDBMS databases serves transactions, reporting, and search, but serves none of them well. In this chalk talk, we'll whiteboard how to decompose a proprietary database into purpose-built layers on AWS, including Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL for transactional workloads, Aurora pgvector for semantic search and GenAI (RAG), and Amazon Redshift via zero-ETL for real-time analytics, for a smarter modernization approach. We'll walk through how this pattern eliminates licensing costs, removes ETL pipelines, and turns your operational data into an AI-ready platform. Come ready to whiteboard your decomposition use case.", "language": "en"},"MAM317-R1": {"abstract": "A monolithic traditional RDBMS databases serves transactions, reporting, and search, but serves none of them well. In this chalk talk, we'll whiteboard how to decompose a proprietary database into purpose-built layers on AWS, including Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL for transactional workloads, Aurora pgvector for semantic search and GenAI (RAG), and Amazon Redshift via zero-ETL for real-time analytics, for a smarter modernization approach. We'll walk through how this pattern eliminates licensing costs, removes ETL pipelines, and turns your operational data into an AI-ready platform. Come ready to whiteboard your decomposition use case.", "language": "en"},"MAM318": {"abstract": "You have hundreds of services stuck on aging infrastructure, and your engineers are spending more time maintaining them than building new experiences. British Airways faced the same challenge with 590 Github repositories and 200 business services on EC2. Using AWS Transform custom, they built an agentic AI platform that autonomously migrates services to ECS Fargate on Graviton, cutting costs by 48% without compromising business logic. They also extended it to improve test coverage and patch security vulnerabilities continuously. In this session, you'll learn how to build a repeatable transformation engine and give your engineers time back.", "language": "en"},"MAM318-SC2": {"abstract": "How do you modernise hundreds of business services without manually re-engineering every one? British Airways is tackling this across 250+ services and 750 code repositories. Using AWS Transform custom, BA is migrating Java services from Amazon EC2 to a containerised, auto-scaling architecture on Amazon ECS Fargate and AWS Graviton. Its repeatable 20-step lifecycle combines deterministic automation and agentic AI with baseline testing, security scanning, and human review. The approach reduces manual effort, validates business logic, and frees engineering capacity for innovation. Discover how BA built its transformation engine and balances AI-driven change with robust engineering controls.", "language": "en"},"MAM319": {"abstract": "Moving servers to the cloud without modernizing the applications on them just moves your technical debt to a new address. LG U+ needed to modernize applications before they could migrate them, and doing both sequentially would have taken too long. In this session, LG U+ shares how they ran AI-powered modernization and migration in parallel across 87 systems spanning 1,579 virtual servers and 107 physical servers. The result: roughly 20% migration velocity improvement and a 50% reduction in Java migration time through AI-assisted refactoring. You'll learn how to modernize at scale without slowing down the move.", "language": "en"},"MAM320": {"abstract": "If your migration is stuck because no one can agree on what moves first while licensing costs compound and dependencies stay undocumented, the problem isn’t willingness. It’s sequencing. Fanatics Commerce had 1800 servers across five data centers and projected 48% infrastructure savings on AWS. Their team shares the structured path: OLA for licensing clarity, DAP for dependency mapping, EBA for organizational alignment, MAP for execution. Walk away with: (1) a concrete OLA-to-MAP sequence, (2) an AI-assisted dependency mapping approach that surfaced connections no one had documented (3) a phased AWS Transform modernization strategy that earns engineering trust before scaling.", "language": "en"},"MAM321-R": {"abstract": "Most ISV monoliths get modernized in three sequential passes: refactor, then multi-tenant, then agentic. Three trips through the same code, each longer than the last. In this chalk talk, we'll dig into the unified refactor pattern that makes tenancy and agentic bets in the same window. We'll explore how data partitioning decisions shift when agents are also a target, when Amazon EKS becomes the substrate for both migrations, and which patterns create more debt than they solve when combined wrong. Leave with a framework for the one refactor window you can afford. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM321-R1": {"abstract": "Most ISV monoliths get modernized in three sequential passes: refactor, then multi-tenant, then agentic. Three trips through the same code, each longer than the last. In this chalk talk, we'll dig into the unified refactor pattern that makes tenancy and agentic bets in the same window. We'll explore how data partitioning decisions shift when agents are also a target, when Amazon EKS becomes the substrate for both migrations, and which patterns create more debt than they solve when combined wrong. Leave with a framework for the one refactor window you can afford. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM322-R": {"abstract": "Modernizing applications is risky without comprehensive test coverage, and most apps that need modernization don't have it. In this workshop, you'll build an AI-powered testing safety net before touching a line of production code. Starting with a deployed insurance application, you'll use Kiro to generate spec-driven tests from source code and Nova Act to discover UI tests through autonomous exploration. Then you'll apply AWS Transform to modernize the codebase and re-run your AI-generated test suite to prove functional equivalence. You'll leave knowing how to de-risk modernization by letting GenAI build your safety net first. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM322-R1": {"abstract": "Modernizing applications is risky without comprehensive test coverage, and most apps that need modernization don't have it. In this workshop, you'll build an AI-powered testing safety net before touching a line of production code. Starting with a deployed insurance application, you'll use Kiro to generate spec-driven tests from source code and Nova Act to discover UI tests through autonomous exploration. Then you'll apply AWS Transform to modernize the codebase and re-run your AI-generated test suite to prove functional equivalence. You'll leave knowing how to de-risk modernization by letting GenAI build your safety net first. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM323-R": {"abstract": "You know your portfolio needs modernization, but which apps go first, and based on what criteria? In this workshop, you'll run the full analyze-prioritize-transform cycle end to end. Using AWS Transform's Agentic Readiness Analysis and Modernization Analysis, you'll evaluate applications from two angles: whether agents can safely reach your logic (API exposure, identity, state, guardrails, observability) and how cloud-native mature your architecture is (compute, data, security, operations). You'll interpret scores, scale across a portfolio with the orchestrator, then close the loop by triggering a containerization transformation on the app that needs it most. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM323-R1": {"abstract": "You know your portfolio needs modernization, but which apps go first, and based on what criteria? In this workshop, you'll run the full analyze-prioritize-transform cycle end to end. Using AWS Transform's Agentic Readiness Analysis and Modernization Analysis, you'll evaluate applications from two angles: whether agents can safely reach your logic (API exposure, identity, state, guardrails, observability) and how cloud-native mature your architecture is (compute, data, security, operations). You'll interpret scores, scale across a portfolio with the orchestrator, then close the loop by triggering a containerization transformation on the app that needs it most. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM324": {"abstract": "Legacy mainframe applications were built for stability, scale, and batch-oriented processing, but they were never designed to power real-time, intelligent, agentic experiences. Modernization changes that. Discover how Nissan reimagined core operations into a cloud-native platform designed for responsiveness, adaptability, and AI-ready workflows. Hear how Bread Financial is evolving beyond credit-processing architectures to accelerate innovation by decomposing monolithic capabilities into bounded context services, creating a modern foundation for autonomous workflows. See how both used AWS Transform to extract business rules from decades-old applications and Kiro to forward-engineer production-ready code. Learn how modernized applications unlock the architecture that makes agentic AI possible.", "language": "en"},"MAM325": {"abstract": "What if you could rapidly migrate your VMware-based workloads to the cloud without giving up control over how you build, configure, and operate your environment? Amazon EVS lets you run the latest VMware Cloud Foundation software within your Amazon VPC using EC2 bare-metal instances. Use the tools and processes your team already knows, now backed by AWS scale and flexibility. Retain control of your virtualization stack, from networking and storage to disaster recovery. We'll walk through deployment workflows and integration patterns with AWS Partners and native AWS services. Hear lessons from a customer who fast-tracked their migration with EVS.", "language": "en"},"MAM326": {"abstract": "Rehosting gets workloads to AWS, but that's just the beginning. This session covers the first 90 days after cutover: stabilizing the environment, building observability so decisions are based on real utilization data instead of pre-migration assumptions, applying auto-scaling and right-sizing adjustments that accelerate ROI, and knowing when a workload is ready to modernize versus when to leave it alone. AWS specialists share the decisions and strategy to turn your freshly migrated environment into one worth the investment.", "language": "en"},"MAM327": {"abstract": "70% of applications still sit on-premises, and the longer they stay, the more tech debt compounds. AWS Transform uses agentic AI to compress the entire data center exit journey from assessment through execution. Start with AI-powered discovery that right-sizes thousands of servers, compares cost scenarios, and builds a business case that gets executive buy-in in days. Move into automated wave planning and landing zone deployment. Then see how network architectures convert into production-ready VPCs and workloads rehost to Amazon EC2 at scale. We follow one customer's real timeline from plan to exit and unpack what made it work.", "language": "en"},"MAM327-SC2": {"abstract": "70% of applications still sit on-premises, and the longer they stay, the more tech debt compounds. AWS Transform uses agentic AI to compress the entire data center exit journey from assessment through execution. Start with AI-powered discovery that right-sizes thousands of servers, compares cost scenarios, and builds a business case that gets executive buy-in in days. Move into automated wave planning and landing zone deployment. See how network architectures convert into production-ready VPCs and workloads rehost to Amazon EC2 at scale. Then hear from StarHub, a leading Singapore-based telecommunications provider, on how agentic AI accelerated their infrastructure modernization and move to AWS in record time.", "language": "en"},"MAM328": {"abstract": "Learn how to achieve enterprise-scale cloud desktop deployment from Capital One, who went from 320 manual provisions per day to 20,000 compliant desktops in 72 hours. Gain production-tested architectural patterns for meeting compliance requirements without slowing delivery. You'll also get a first look at the latest WorkSpaces innovations and our vision for the future of cloud desktops, including how we're expanding what's possible for IT teams managing modern workloads at scale. This session is for those migrating from VDI, scaling an existing fleet, or planning for what's next.", "language": "en"},"MAM329-R": {"abstract": "Migrating Microsoft workloads to AWS requires rethinking your monitoring strategy. Existing observability approaches may not translate seamlessly to the cloud, creating blind spots that lead to costly downtime and degraded end-user experiences. In this chalk talk, we'll explore how to strengthen your observability posture as you migrate .NET applications, SQL Server databases, and Windows services to AWS. We'll cover how to use AWS-native and open-source tooling to monitor workloads across VMs, containers, and serverless, giving you confidence to migrate faster while maintaining operational excellence. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM329-R1": {"abstract": "Migrating Microsoft workloads to AWS requires rethinking your monitoring strategy. Existing observability approaches may not translate seamlessly to the cloud, creating blind spots that lead to costly downtime and degraded end-user experiences. In this chalk talk, we'll explore how to strengthen your observability posture as you migrate .NET applications, SQL Server databases, and Windows services to AWS. We'll cover how to use AWS-native and open-source tooling to monitor workloads across VMs, containers, and serverless, giving you confidence to migrate faster while maintaining operational excellence. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM330": {"abstract": "Dive deep into the architectural decisions that shape a resilient, high-performing VMware environment on Amazon EVS. Explore VCF 9 support, Windows Server license-included entitlements, networking designs, storage configurations tuned for performance and cost, and operational patterns for backup, patching, and disaster recovery. Hear from a customer running production workloads on EVS and leave with actionable architectures tailored to your VMware workloads.", "language": "en"},"MAM331-R": {"abstract": "Reimagine what migration looks like when landing zone setup and network translation go from weeks to hours. In this chalk talk, we show how AWS Transform's agentic AI compresses that timeline, from migration inventory to fully deployed, validated landing zones and modernized networks. See how production-ready account structures deploy through Control Tower with guardrails in place, and how firewall configurations become optimized VPCs, subnets, and security groups. Bring your questions and hear from the experts building these capabilities.", "language": "en"},"MAM331-R1": {"abstract": "Reimagine what migration looks like when landing zone setup and network translation go from weeks to hours. In this chalk talk, we show how AWS Transform's agentic AI compresses that timeline, from migration inventory to fully deployed, validated landing zones and modernized networks. See how production-ready account structures deploy through Control Tower with guardrails in place, and how firewall configurations become optimized VPCs, subnets, and security groups. Bring your questions and hear from the experts building these capabilities.", "language": "en"},"MAM332-R": {"abstract": "You rely on desktop and mainframe applications for critical workflows, but these interfaces remain inaccessible to AI agents. Your Robotic Process Automation efforts have struggled to keep pace as applications and configurations constantly change. Amazon WorkSpaces lets AI agents securely operate the same desktop and mainframe applications your employees use, without any application modernization. WorkSpaces supports Model Context Protocol (MCP), so it works with any agent framework. In this workshop, connect to a pre-provisioned WorkSpace, build a custom agent, run agents that complete desktop workflows, and monitor agent sessions with CloudWatch and CloudTrail. Bring laptop to participate.", "language": "en"},"MAM332-R1": {"abstract": "You rely on desktop and mainframe applications for critical workflows, but these interfaces remain inaccessible to AI agents. Your Robotic Process Automation efforts have struggled to keep pace as applications and configurations constantly change. Amazon WorkSpaces lets AI agents securely operate the same desktop and mainframe applications your employees use, without any application modernization. WorkSpaces supports Model Context Protocol (MCP), so it works with any agent framework. In this workshop, connect to a pre-provisioned WorkSpace, build a custom agent, run agents that complete desktop workflows, and monitor agent sessions with CloudWatch and CloudTrail. Bring laptop to participate.", "language": "en"},"MAM333": {"abstract": "Critical business data remains locked inside SAP ERP and BW systems, limiting real-time insights and AI-driven automation. In this hands-on workshop, learn how to break down data silos using a modern, cost-effective architecture without expensive ETL pipelines. Explore a unified analytics strategy spanning Databricks, Snowflake, and AWS-native services that enables end-to-end SAP data modernization. Then, build with the AWS for SAP MCP Server, enabling agentic AI to orchestrate across SAP, Salesforce, and AWS without writing code.", "language": "en"},"MAM334": {"abstract": "Enterprise processes span SAP for ERP, Salesforce for CRM, and ServiceNow for ITSM, connected by aging, brittle integrations that are slow to change. Agentic AI offers a better path: replacing point-to-point integrations with agents that reason across applications. In this workshop, you modernize an SAP-centric business process by orchestrating Amazon Bedrock AgentCore agents over Model Context Protocol, including the AWS for SAP MCP Server. You implement cross-application use cases spanning finance, supply chain, and operations then leave with a deployable reference architecture for moving from custom integrations to agent-orchestrated workflows.", "language": "en"},"MAM335-S": {"abstract": "What if modernization started beyond the code? SoftServe is reimagining application modernization by working backwards from business needs and desired outcomes to determine what should change and why. In this session, see how SoftServe Agentic Application Modernization combines this outcome-driven approach with CAST Software, AWS Transform, Kiro, AI-DLC and specialized AI agents to accelerate discovery, assessment, transformation, and validation. Learn how SoftServe provides the AI foundation to orchestrate and govern these agents, turning modernization into an intelligent, repeatable journey that enables AI for organizations, connects business intent with technology decisions and execution on AWS. This presentation is brought to you by SoftServe, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"MAM336": {"abstract": "Full legacy application rewrites take years. Agentic AI lets you deliver value now. In this code talk, we build an AI agent that wraps an existing legacy application without changing the core system. You'll see how the agent understands user intent, calls existing application functions, and helps users complete business tasks through a modern conversational experience. Ask questions as we go from legacy to AI-assisted workflow in real time. You'll leave ready to put agentic AI in front of your legacy application today.", "language": "en"},"MAM336-R": {"abstract": "Full legacy application rewrites take years. Agentic AI lets you deliver value now. In this code talk, we build an AI agent that wraps an existing legacy application without changing the core system. You'll see how the agent understands user intent, calls existing application functions, and helps users complete business tasks through a modern conversational experience. Ask questions as we go from legacy to AI-assisted workflow in real time. You'll leave ready to put agentic AI in front of your legacy application today.", "language": "en"},"MAM336-R1": {"abstract": "Full legacy application rewrites take years. Agentic AI lets you deliver value now. In this code talk, we build an AI agent that wraps an existing legacy application without changing the core system. You'll see how the agent understands user intent, calls existing application functions, and helps users complete business tasks through a modern conversational experience. Ask questions as we go from legacy to AI-assisted workflow in real time. You'll leave ready to put agentic AI in front of your legacy application today.", "language": "en"},"MAM337": {"abstract": "Modernizing SQL Server and its dependent .NET applications to Aurora PostgreSQL typically requires months of manual effort across schema conversion, stored procedure rewriting, and application code changes. In this code talk, see how AWS Transform uses agentic AI to automate this journey end-to-end. Through a live walkthrough, we'll showcase complex schema transformations, T-SQL to PL/pgSQL stored procedure conversions, Entity Framework provider updates, and wave-based orchestration of multi-database estates with human-in-the-loop validation checkpoints. Ask questions throughout. Leave with patterns for modernizing SQL Server at scale.", "language": "en"},"MAM338-S": {"abstract": "Learn how LPL Financial built an always-on trading platform on AWS that supports 32,000+ financial advisors with resilient, multi-region architecture for mission-critical, latency-sensitive workloads. Discover how a unified data foundation across trading, brokerage, and custodial systems creates a trusted layer for innovation, and learn the realities of deploying agentic AI in a regulated broker-dealer environment. Gain practical insights into architecture patterns, governance, real-time data access, key tradeoffs, and lessons learned that can help accelerate your own modernization and AI initiatives. This presentation is brought to you by Cognizant, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"MAM339": {"abstract": "Enterprises run hundreds of applications from ERP, CRM, supply chain, and beyond and yet orchestrating intelligent actions across these systems remains a challenge. In this chalk talk, learn how to architect and manage cross-enterprise agentic orchestration using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. We explore how Model Context Protocol (MCP) and Agent-to-Agent (A2A) communication enable AI agents to seamlessly interact across application boundaries through a single, unified chat interface. Walk away with practical architecture patterns for connecting SAP and adjacent enterprise systems like SalesForce, ServicesNow etc into a cohesive, AI-powered automation layer", "language": "en"},"MAM342": {"abstract": "Bayer's R&D analytics relied on manual pipelines, fragmented tooling, and engineering-heavy workflows that bottlenecked scientists. In this session, hear how Bayer modernized that stack into an agentic decision engine on AWS, cutting token costs by roughly 600% and saving scientists 70% of their engineering time. We'll trace the modernization journey from legacy analytics architecture through the migration to cloud-native services and show how that foundation enabled autonomous multi-agent workflows that now orchestrate R&D decisions at enterprise scale. Leave with a framework for modernizing analytics into agentic AI capabilities.", "language": "en"},"MAM343": {"abstract": "Your most valuable business processes often run inside desktop applications and mainframes that expose no APIs for AI agents to call. In this session, learn how to use Amazon WorkSpaces to give agents a governed desktop where they operate these applications directly, just as an employee would. In this chalk talk, we'll dig into scoping what agents are permitted to do, auditing agent actions, and configuring agent identity. We'll walk through strategies for agent optimization: how to choose the right agent tools, select the right model for your workflow, and build reusable agent skills. Applied together, these techniques cut task time, lower cost, and increase the accuracy of your agent workflows.", "language": "en"},"MAM344": {"abstract": "Learn how agentic AI is transforming enterprise modernization from one-off projects into an always-on practice. In this session, we explore how organizations are accelerating cloud migration, modernizing mainframe, Windows, and custom applications, and continuously reducing tech debt across their entire portfolio, evolving their pipelines from CI/CD to CI/CD/CM (continuous modernization). See how teams are compressing modernization timelines from years to months while keeping codebases current and AI-ready. Hear from product leader Neha Goswami on the latest innovations and what's ahead.", "language": "en"},"MAM346": {"abstract": "Transaction Network Services (TNS) needed to modernize their Altitude payments platform that included 274 projects, 988K lines of code, and 20 years of legacy .NET Framework to .NET 10. Their estimate: six months. The result: two days, 26 modules migrated, and 34 security vulnerabilities resolved. In this session, you'll learn what made it possible - from upgrading shared libraries first, running deterministic tools before AI, using human-verified tests, to keeping engineers on the keyboard after the tools stop running. Walk away with a practical, repeatable playbook for accelerating large-scale .NET modernization.", "language": "en"},"MAM347": {"abstract": "Whether you run WorkSpaces today or are evaluating cloud desktops for the first time, operational overhead follows every virtual desktop deployment: ongoing monitoring, systemic issues that surface as tickets, and end-user requests that consume administrator time. Most teams operate reactively, triaging problems after they surface and manually guiding users through resolution. This session explores how Amazon WorkSpaces Advisor is using AI to reduce resolution time for both IT administrators and end users. We'll walk through the operational challenges we're hearing from customers, share our approach to solving them, and demonstrate early results from production environments. Bring your deployment architecture questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM347-R": {"abstract": "Whether you run WorkSpaces today or are evaluating cloud desktops for the first time, operational overhead follows every virtual desktop deployment: ongoing monitoring, systemic issues that surface as tickets, and end-user requests that consume administrator time. Most teams operate reactively, triaging problems after they surface and manually guiding users through resolution. This session explores how Amazon WorkSpaces Advisor is using AI to reduce resolution time for both IT administrators and end users. We'll walk through the operational challenges we're hearing from customers, share our approach to solving them, and demonstrate early results from production environments. Bring your deployment architecture questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM347-R1": {"abstract": "Whether you run WorkSpaces today or are evaluating cloud desktops for the first time, operational overhead follows every virtual desktop deployment: ongoing monitoring, systemic issues that surface as tickets, and end-user requests that consume administrator time. Most teams operate reactively, triaging problems after they surface and manually guiding users through resolution. This session explores how Amazon WorkSpaces Advisor is using AI to reduce resolution time for both IT administrators and end users. We'll walk through the operational challenges we're hearing from customers, share our approach to solving them, and demonstrate early results from production environments. Bring your deployment architecture questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM348": {"abstract": "Builders lose days configuring environments. IT teams struggle to govern the growing sprawl of AI tools and extensions across their organization. In this session, we explore these challenges and share how Amazon WorkSpaces is approaching the builder desktop experience. We'll discuss what enterprises need to provision environments faster, maintain governance across multiple surfaces, and keep pace as AI-assisted development becomes the norm. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM348-R": {"abstract": "Builders lose days configuring environments. IT teams struggle to govern the growing sprawl of AI tools and extensions across their organization. In this session, we explore these challenges and share how Amazon WorkSpaces is approaching the builder desktop experience. We'll discuss what enterprises need to provision environments faster, maintain governance across multiple surfaces, and keep pace as AI-assisted development becomes the norm. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM348-R1": {"abstract": "Builders lose days configuring environments. IT teams struggle to govern the growing sprawl of AI tools and extensions across their organization. In this session, we explore these challenges and share how Amazon WorkSpaces is approaching the builder desktop experience. We'll discuss what enterprises need to provision environments faster, maintain governance across multiple surfaces, and keep pace as AI-assisted development becomes the norm. Bring your questions.", "language": "en"},"MAM349": {"abstract": "Legacy application modernization is a coordination and code generation problem. A large application must be understood, verified, and integrated without losing fidelity. AWS Transform for mainframe reads legacy code and extracts its business rules into traceable specifications that describe what the application does. Learn how AWS Transform overcomes this modernization challenge, and discover the latest capabilities for scaling modernization that compress delivery from days to hours.", "language": "en"},"MAM349-SC2": {"abstract": "Legacy application modernization is a coordination and code generation problem. A large application must be understood, verified, and integrated without losing fidelity. AWS Transform for mainframe reads legacy code and extracts its business rules into traceable specifications that describe what the application does. Learn how AWS Transform overcomes this modernization challenge, and discover the latest capabilities for scaling modernization that compress delivery from days to hours.", "language": "en"},"MAM350": {"abstract": "In this Code Talk, learn how continuous modernization enables faster tech debt analysis and remediation by starting directly from your cloud accounts. Instead of manually connecting code repositories upfront, you can begin identifying tech debt immediately using lifecycle-event signals from your cloud environment. The platform then provides an easy path to resolution with automatic generation of pull requests. We will walk through the account-first workflow and how it gets you from discovery to remediation faster with less setup.", "language": "en"},"MAM350-R": {"abstract": "In this Code Talk, learn how continuous modernization enables faster tech debt analysis and remediation by starting directly from your cloud accounts. Instead of manually connecting code repositories upfront, you can begin identifying tech debt immediately using lifecycle-event signals from your cloud environment. The platform then provides an easy path to resolution with automatic generation of pull requests. We will walk through the account-first workflow and how it gets you from discovery to remediation faster with less setup.", "language": "en"},"MAM350-R1": {"abstract": "In this Code Talk, see how continuous modernization keeps tech debt under control across your application estate. After a one-time setup, it continuously detects outdated runtimes, deprecated libraries, and security vulnerabilities, using signals from both your cloud environment and your code. It then fixes them at scale with automatically generated pull requests. We'll go live through real scenarios, from discovery to remediation, and show how scheduled scans catch new tech debt before it piles up.", "language": "en"},"MAM401": {"abstract": "Can your Windows Server applications and SQL Server databases survive a system outage? In this builders' session, you'll find out by building and testing HA/DR architectures against simulated failures. Get hands-on experience with Elastic Disaster Recovery and Systems Manager to construct resilient infrastructure and recovery automation. Measure RTO and RPO in real time as you purposely break production workloads. Explore additional topics like RDS, S3, Elastic Beanstalk, and AWS Managed AD. You'll leave with a validated resiliency blueprint and the confidence to protect your most critical Microsoft workloads.", "language": "en"},"MAM403-R": {"abstract": "Enterprise architects face a critical challenge: breaking monolithic database-centric applications into microservices while managing risk and cost. Where do you draw domain boundaries? How do you extract 20 years of business logic from stored procedures into the application layer? This chalk talk reveals the two-layer decomposition strategy—combining database structure and runtime execution patterns—to identify service boundaries. Leveraging AWS Transform and Kiro, collapse months of manual analysis, design and development into hours of executable code. Through live whiteboarding, learn the data-driven framework enabling business logic extraction, independent deployment, licensing cost reduction, and faster modernization.", "language": "en"},"MAM403-R1": {"abstract": "Enterprise architects face a critical challenge: breaking monolithic database-centric applications into microservices while managing risk and cost. Where do you draw domain boundaries? How do you extract 20 years of business logic from stored procedures into the application layer? This chalk talk reveals the two-layer decomposition strategy—combining database structure and runtime execution patterns—to identify service boundaries. Leveraging AWS Transform and Kiro, collapse months of manual analysis, design and development into hours of executable code. Through live whiteboarding, learn the data-driven framework enabling business logic extraction, independent deployment, licensing cost reduction, and faster modernization.", "language": "en"},"MAM405": {"abstract": "Lift-and-shift gets you to the cloud, but it doesn't solve the licensing costs that follow. In this builders' session, you'll work through four labs to reduce your Windows and SQL Server spend on Amazon EC2: (1) enable Compute Optimizer for continuous fleet right-sizing; (2) use Optimize CPU to align cores with compute requirements; (3) classify SQL Server HA clusters to remove passive-node licensing fees; and (4) downgrade SQL Server Enterprise to Standard edition. Leave with a production-ready cost optimization blueprint.", "language": "en"},"MAM406": {"abstract": "Moving workloads from Windows to Linux and SQL Server to PostgreSQL has always been a complex, multi-step project. Agentic AI changes the game by orchestrating the entire journey for you. In this expert-level workshop, you'll start with on-premises Windows Server workloads in a simulated data center and migrate to Amazon EC2 covering agent installation, continuous replication, and cutover. Then you'll modernize by upgrading SQL Server to PostgreSQL and migrating PHP to Amazon EKS, applying replatforming patterns in practice. You'll leave with end-to-end experience executing OS and database modernization, accelerated by agentic AI. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM407-R": {"abstract": "Forward-looking organizations aren't just migrating to AWS — they're using migration to transform their entire security posture. In this workshop, your workloads have just landed on AWS and you'll immediately secure them using sandbox accounts. You'll use Amazon GuardDuty to detect runtime-level threats and malware, Amazon Inspector to prioritize software vulnerabilities, and AWS Security Hub to correlate findings into actionable exposures. You'll finish by building an automated remediation pipeline that isolates compromised resources without human intervention. Leave with a repeatable Day 1 security playbook for any migrated workload. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM407-R1": {"abstract": "Forward-looking organizations aren't just migrating to AWS — they're using migration to transform their entire security posture. In this workshop, your workloads have just landed on AWS and you'll immediately secure them using sandbox accounts. You'll use Amazon GuardDuty to detect runtime-level threats and malware, Amazon Inspector to prioritize software vulnerabilities, and AWS Security Hub to correlate findings into actionable exposures. You'll finish by building an automated remediation pipeline that isolates compromised resources without human intervention. Leave with a repeatable Day 1 security playbook for any migrated workload. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM408": {"abstract": "Designing landing zones and translating on-premises networks into cloud-native architectures is complex and time-consuming. AWS Transform automates both. In this workshop, you'll see the landing zone agent analyze your requirements and deploy AWS Control Tower, organizational units, service control policies, and workload accounts as infrastructure as code. Then the network agent translates VMware networking components or firewall configurations into VPCs, subnets, security groups, and transit gateways with hub-and-spoke or isolated topologies, ready for deployment in CDK or Terraform modules. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM409": {"abstract": "Oracle modernization promises freedom from licensing, lock-in, and operational overhead, yet projects stall on PL/SQL packages, schema quirks, and application logic that resists automated translation. In this workshop, you'll migrate a live Oracle workload to open-source Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL end-to-end and tackle the hardest schema conversion challenges that derail real-world projects. You'll work through PL/SQL translation, dependency resolution, and validation using AWS agentic AI.", "language": "en"},"MAM411": {"abstract": "As organizations look to reduce tech debt for their .NET applications, builders are looking to accelerate modernization with AI tools. In this hands-on session, we'll explore best practices for modernizing .NET Framework applications with AWS Transform. You'll learn how to work alongside the agent to reach a desired outcome. Together, we will apply plan customizations, steering documents, checkpoints, and iteration. Come ready to share your use cases and leave with practical steps to efficient, cost-effective modernization. Bring your laptop with Visual Studio and an AWS account onboarded to AWS Transform.", "language": "en"},"MAM412": {"abstract": "Most modernization teams bolt security on as an afterthought, creating costly late-stage vulnerabilities. In this code talk, you'll follow along as we build a custom agent using Strands Agents SDK on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore that takes a security-first approach. We wire up AWS Transform agents for tech debt analysis via MCP integrations, connect AWS Continuum for deep code-level vulnerability scanning, and orchestrate everything through Kiro. The result: an agent that synthesizes a security-hardened modernization plan and autonomously executes it. See AI agents collaborate in real time to transform and secure code simultaneously, eliminating handoffs between teams.", "language": "en"},"MAM412-R": {"abstract": "Most modernization teams bolt security on as an afterthought, creating costly late-stage vulnerabilities. In this code talk, you'll follow along as we build a custom agent using Strands Agents SDK on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore that takes a security-first approach. We wire up AWS Transform agents for tech debt analysis via MCP integrations, connect AWS Continuum for deep code-level vulnerability scanning, and orchestrate everything through Kiro. The result: an agent that synthesizes a security-hardened modernization plan and autonomously executes it. See AI agents collaborate in real time to transform and secure code simultaneously, eliminating handoffs between teams.", "language": "en"},"MAM412-R1": {"abstract": "Most modernization teams bolt security on as an afterthought, creating costly late-stage vulnerabilities. In this code talk, you'll follow along as we build a custom agent using Strands Agents SDK on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore that takes a security-first approach. We wire up AWS Transform agents for tech debt analysis via MCP integrations, connect AWS Continuum for deep code-level vulnerability scanning, and orchestrate everything through Kiro. The result: an agent that synthesizes a security-hardened modernization plan and autonomously executes it. See AI agents collaborate in real time to transform and secure code simultaneously, eliminating handoffs between teams.", "language": "en"},"MAM413-R": {"abstract": "Running multi-tenant agents on Kubernetes gives you flexibility, but it introduces certain operational overhead like cluster management, scaling decisions, and identity plumbing. In this workshop, you'll migrate agents to Amazon Bedrock AgentCore's serverless infrastructure without giving up isolation or control. Starting from a working agentic SaaS application on Amazon EKS, you'll progressively refactor each component onto AgentCore: implement tenant isolation, configure shared MCP tools with per-tenant scoping, and instrument tenant-aware memory and observability. You'll validate tenant separation at every step and leave with hands-on experience moving multi-tenant agent infrastructure to a managed architecture. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM413-R1": {"abstract": "Running multi-tenant agents on Kubernetes gives you flexibility, but it introduces certain operational overhead like cluster management, scaling decisions, and identity plumbing. In this workshop, you'll migrate agents to Amazon Bedrock AgentCore's serverless infrastructure without giving up isolation or control. Starting from a working agentic SaaS application on Amazon EKS, you'll progressively refactor each component onto AgentCore: implement tenant isolation, configure shared MCP tools with per-tenant scoping, and instrument tenant-aware memory and observability. You'll validate tenant separation at every step and leave with hands-on experience moving multi-tenant agent infrastructure to a managed architecture. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM414": {"abstract": "How do you modernize thousands of applications concurrently to meet aggressive migration timelines? In this chalk talk, we'll work through architectural patterns for scaling AWS Transform with CI/CD integration: parallel processing with serverless compute, programmatic orchestration via APIs, container strategies, observability at scale, and campaign coordination across teams. Bring your use case and whiteboard it with us. Whether you need pipeline integration, secure private repo processing, or a self-service modernization platform, we'll design your architecture together.", "language": "en"},"MAM415": {"abstract": "Organizations facing VMware licensing pressure need more than a migration plan. They need a structured exit strategy spanning assessment, mobilization, migration, and modernization. In this session, we discuss how AWS Transform drives business outcomes at each phase: portfolio assessment that quantifies TCO reduction, wave planning that protects application uptime, automated cutover orchestration that eliminates risk, and post-migration modernization that captures cloud-native savings. Drawing from real-world examples, we explore how teams compressed 18-month timelines into ten or lower using AWS Transform and agentic capabilities for migrating compute, database and storage resources, then open the discussion to address your specific use cases.", "language": "en"},"MAM416": {"abstract": "This workshop walks you through modernizing a .NET Framework 4.8 Web Forms application to cross-platform .NET 10. You will learn how to transform a .NET Framework 4.8 Web Forms application to .NET 10 Blazor using AWS Transform Interactive Mode. Throughout the session, you will interact with the AI agent in real-time asking questions, reviewing assessment and transformation plans, and examining transformation results, including code diffs and build verification. Finally, use Kiro to identify and fix post-transformation runtime issues, such as layout problems, and containerize and deploy the transformed application to Amazon ECS Fargate using the Kiro IDE.", "language": "en"},"MAM417": {"abstract": "Modernizing Microsoft workloads means tackling .NET and SQL Server together, not as separate projects. In this workshop, you'll use AWS Transform to compress this effort into a single sprint and reduce operating costs by up to 70% by moving off costly licenses. Working from a legacy app, you'll port .NET Framework code to modern, cross-platform .NET, migrate SQL Server to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, then containerize and deploy to Amazon ECS or EKS. You'll leave with a proven approach to transform your full stack into a scalable, cloud-native architecture. Come ready with your personal GitHub account. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM417-R": {"abstract": "Modernizing Microsoft workloads means tackling .NET and SQL Server together, not as separate projects. In this workshop, you'll use AWS Transform to compress this effort into a single sprint and reduce operating costs by up to 70% by moving off costly licenses. Working from a legacy app, you'll port .NET Framework code to modern, cross-platform .NET, migrate SQL Server to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, then containerize and deploy to Amazon ECS or EKS. You'll leave with a proven approach to transform your full stack into a scalable, cloud-native architecture. Come ready with your personal GitHub account. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM417-R1": {"abstract": "Modernizing Microsoft workloads means tackling .NET and SQL Server together, not as separate projects. In this workshop, you'll use AWS Transform to compress this effort into a single sprint and reduce operating costs by up to 70% by moving off costly licenses. Working from a legacy app, you'll port .NET Framework code to modern, cross-platform .NET, migrate SQL Server to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, then containerize and deploy to Amazon ECS or EKS. You'll leave with a proven approach to transform your full stack into a scalable, cloud-native architecture. Come ready with your personal GitHub account. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM418": {"abstract": "SAP operations teams spend hours sifting through thousands of log lines to diagnose outages, often only after business impact has occurred. In this workshop, learn how to implement AI-powered operations for SAP workloads on AWS, whether customer-managed or RISE with SAP. Ingest SAP system logs into Amazon CloudWatch using the CloudWatch Agent and SAP ECS LogServ, then apply Amazon Bedrock–powered agents for proactive analysis and reactive root-cause investigation. See how AWS DevOps Agent extends this with autonomous remediation. Leave with a deployable architecture, real customer examples, and guidance to get started in days.", "language": "en"},"MAM419-R": {"abstract": "Legacy applications on outdated frameworks and deprecated runtimes represent a growing modernization challenge. In this workshop, use AWS Transform custom to build and execute transformations that accelerate Java modernization at scale. You'll define transformation rules using natural language and code examples, execute multi-step upgrades (Java 8 to 21, Spring Boot 2 to 3, Jakarta EE), refine quality through the agentic AI feedback loop, validate with built-in testing, and run campaigns across multiple repositories. You'll leave with reusable transformation definitions you can apply to your own Java codebases. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM419-R1": {"abstract": "Legacy applications on outdated frameworks and deprecated runtimes represent a growing modernization challenge. In this workshop, use AWS Transform custom to build and execute transformations that accelerate Java modernization at scale. You'll define transformation rules using natural language and code examples, execute multi-step upgrades (Java 8 to 21, Spring Boot 2 to 3, Jakarta EE), refine quality through the agentic AI feedback loop, validate with built-in testing, and run campaigns across multiple repositories. You'll leave with reusable transformation definitions you can apply to your own Java codebases. Laptop required.", "language": "en"},"MAM420-S": {"abstract": "Moving a database from on-premises to the cloud is easy to get wrong: undersized instances, surprise costs, unplanned downtime. Join Kellyn and John as we look at Redgate Monitor's new database migration planning feature, designed to help you size, plan, and cost a move with real data instead of guesswork. We will also explore how Redgate Monitor is evolving to support the next generation of database operations, supporting teams who are using AI assistants and Agents who need access to observability data quickly, giving operational staff faster answers and smarter recommendations when managing complex database systems. This presentation is brought to you by Red Gate, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"MUP101": {"abstract": "Ready to accelerate your organization's cloud journey? Discover how leading companies are closing the cloud skills gap through innovative upskilling strategies that deliver real results. Learn practical approaches for building cloud capabilities across your organization, from creating internal champions to measuring success. Connect with peers, share experiences, and leave with actionable strategies.", "language": "en"},"MUP102": {"abstract": "This meetup is tailored for early career professionals looking to kickstart their cloud computing careers. Attendees can engage with AWS experts and community members to discuss topics such as breaking into the industry, leveraging AWS certifications, and building practical skills and networks to enhance their employability. The meetup can also cover internship and job opportunities, as well as strategies for navigating the early stages of a cloud-focused career.", "language": "en"},"MUP103": {"abstract": "Migration and modernization programs are usually justified by cost and agility. They are also a good moment to lower carbon emissions and prepare for generative AI. Sustainability and GenAI are often planned separately from the migration itself, and that can mean duplicated work later. This session looks at how organizations can bring all three goals into one modernization plan on AWS. We will cover how to set a carbon baseline with the AWS Customer Carbon Footprint Tool and which modernization choices tend to lower emissions, such as AWS Graviton, managed and serverless services, storage lifecycle policies, and Region selection. We will also look at how GenAI can speed up migration work like code analysis and transformation, and how a modern data and application foundation makes GenAI adoption easier afterward. Attendees will compare approaches, share what has worked in their own organizations, and leave with practical ideas for making sustainability and GenAI part of their modernization roadmap.", "language": "en"},"MUP105": {"abstract": "Experience-Based Acceleration (EBA) is emerging as a powerful approach for organizations starting their AI agent journey. Through AWS AI services and tools, teams can rapidly prototype and implement agentic solutions that deliver tangible results. This meetup explores practical strategies for designing, building, and scaling AI agent MVPs in less than 6 weeks, focusing on real-world implementations that boost productivity and automate workflows while achieving measurable business outcomes.", "language": "en"},"MUP106": {"abstract": "In retail, every interaction shapes the customer experience across the entire shopping journey, and it all intensifies at peak season. The edge is knowing where AI agents can scale and where a human agent protects the experience. Sit down with peers facing the same challenges and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP107": {"abstract": "In financial services, every interaction has to earn trust, meet compliance, and deepen the customer relationship. The hard part is knowing where AI agents can take the lead and where a human agent should step in. Sit down with peers facing the same challenges and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP108": {"abstract": "In travel and hospitality, every interaction shapes the guest experience, and loyalty is often won or lost the moment plans change. That is where AI agents need to perform like your best agents and where a human agent still matters most. Sit down with peers facing the same challenges and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP109": {"abstract": "In insurance, every interaction is a moment of truth for the policyholder relationship, from the first question to the hardest claim. The whole game is knowing where AI agents can take the lead and where a human agent should. Sit down with peers facing the same challenges and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP110": {"abstract": "Plenty of agentic CX pilots work. Far fewer make it into production across the business. What separates the two is the conversation we want to have. Sit down with peers moving from pilot to full adoption and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon", "language": "en"},"MUP111": {"abstract": "Every agentic CX team has to decide where AI agents take the lead and where a human agent should step in. Getting that balance right drives both adoption and return. Sit down with peers making those calls and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP112": {"abstract": "The most useful lessons in agentic CX come from what didn't go to plan. Sit down with peers who have been through pilots, rollouts, and ROI reviews, and trade honest answers on what worked, what didn't, and what they would change. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP113": {"abstract": "Everyone is building agentic CX. Far fewer have gotten it adopted and proven what it returns. That gap, from pilot to full adoption to measurable ROI, is exactly the conversation we want to have. Sit down with peers facing the same challenges and compare notes on what is working, what isn't, and what they would do differently. Amazon Connect Customer experts will help facilitate, alongside our agentic CX ROI expert and leaders who have scaled AI adoption inside Amazon.", "language": "en"},"MUP114": {"abstract": "Enterprise customers pay for cloud services across dozens of payer accounts and countries through procurement/accounts payable platforms like SAP Ariba and Coupa and track it all in spreadsheets and email threads. Purchase orders run out unnoticed. Payments land on the wrong invoices. Disputes take months. In this session, see how a new first-party application gives Accounts Payable teams one live view of purchase orders, invoices and payments matched against billing records - no console login required.", "language": "en"},"MUP202": {"abstract": "Coding agents can turn an idea into a working prototype in an afternoon. When building gets cheap, the hard part of product work moves to deciding what is worth building, and why. Join product managers, founders and builders for an open conversation on how product work is changing: discovery, prioritization, measurement and working with engineering when agents do much of the building. Share what has worked for you, what broke, and what you are still figuring out. No slides and no pitch, just peers, a whiteboard and real experiences.", "language": "en"},"MUP204": {"abstract": "Everyone wants AI agents in production. But most enterprise apps were built long before agents existed. Their APIs are hard to discover, auth wasn't designed for machine callers, and few systems recover safely when an agent retries a call. Join peers working through this right now for an open conversation. We'll swap real experiences on finding readiness gaps in your code with tools like AWS Transform, deciding what to modernize first, and choosing where agents make sense versus simple automation. Bring your challenges, wins, and lessons learned. No slides, just honest discussion with people solving the same problem.", "language": "en"},"MUP206": {"abstract": "Meet the Kiro Ambassadors at re:Invent and hear how they build real things with Kiro. They will share how they work with agentic coding day to day and what they have learned shipping their own projects, and you are invited to jump in with your own questions and experiences. A relaxed chat to swap insights with the people using Kiro and meet other builders on campus.", "language": "en"},"MUP208": {"abstract": "AI is reshaping how we build, invest, and lead, and women in tech have an opportunity to shape what comes next. Join AWS women leaders and allies for an open conversation on three questions: Which AI trends matter most for 2027? Where should you and your organization invest your time and budget? Which skills will set you apart as agents take on more of the work? We will build a shared map on the whiteboard, swap career stories, and connect with peers. Everyone is welcome. Leave with new connections and a concrete next step for your AI journey.", "language": "en"},"MUP209": {"abstract": "Resilience is a shared responsibility between AWS and customers, and clear ownership keeps recovery on track. This session walks through the AWS resilience toolkit. We cover Next Generation AWS Resilience Hub, which uses GenAI-powered failure mode assessments to evaluate workload posture, Application Recovery Controller, and AWS Fault Injection Service for controlled, repeatable failure testing. We also cover the programs that help customers adopt them such as Resilience Program Accelerator and the Resiliency Core Program. Through real examples from AWS and customers, attendees leave with a model for ownership, a prioritized test plan, and a roadmap to improve their resilience posture.", "language": "en"}};
  window.APP_DATA.sessions.forEach(function (s) {
    var x = m[s.session_id];
    if (x) for (var k in x) if (x[k]) s[k] = x[k];
  });
})();
